      "theory": "The Treaty of Detroit (1950) established the post-war industrial social contract: guaranteed wage increases indexed to productivity and cost-of-living, health benefits, and pensions in exchange for labor peace. In 1950, American manufacturing output represented nearly 50% of world industrial production, anchoring an expanding middle class.",
