      "id": "15-train-your-replacement-the-h-1b-blues",
      "title": "Train Your Replacement (The H-1B Blues)",
      "act": "Act IV: The Slaughter (2025–Present)",
      "actNumber": 4,
      "audioFile": "assets/audio/15-train-your-replacement-the-h-1b-blues.mp3",
      "tagline": "Knowledge Extraction & The 30-Day Transition Ultimatum",
      "leadArchetype": "The Veteran Knowledge Worker / Guest Worker",
      "tempo": "95 BPM",
      "key": "D Minor",
      "style": "Slow-Burn Electric Blues / Modern Protest Ballad",
      "theory": "Contingent severance agreements mandating that laid-off domestic employees train foreign guest workers or fine-tune algorithmic models as a legal prerequisite for receiving severance pay and health insurance continuation—a direct modern manifestation of captive labor extraction.",
      "summary": "This is the emotional nadir of the album. The Son has been fired (Track 14), but he cannot leave yet. To receive his severance package, he is legally required to spend his final 30 days training his replacement1. This track details the excruciating intimacy of teaching a stranger—often a visa holder who is also being exploited—how to do the job you loved. It captures the specific humiliation of \"showing him the password\" and explaining the \"legacy code\"2. The music is a tragic, slow-burning Industrial Blues, blending the acoustic guitar of the father with the cold, mechanical noise of the server room.",
      "cleanLyrics": "[Verse 1]\nHe sits in my chair and he breathes my air\nHe adjusts the height and he combs his hair\nHe smiles at me with a nervous shake\nHe knows exactly what is at stake\nHe calls me \"Sir\" and he holds a pen\nTo write down the wisdom of the older men\nI have thirty days to show him the keys\nOr I lose my check and I lose my knees\n\n[Chorus]\nTrain your replacement\nSign the decree\nGive him the fruit of your memory\nShow him the password, show him the code\nShow him the map of the heavy load\nHe costs a third of what I made a year\nAnd he is the reason that I disappear\nThe H-1B Blues\n\n[Verse 2]\nI open the file that I wrote in '10\nAnd I walk him through the logic again\n\"Be careful here, this server is old\nIt holds the data like a pot of gold\"\nHe nods his head and he types it fast\nDeleting my future to secure his past\nI don't hate the kid, he's just trying to eat\nBut it's hard to be the ground beneath his feet\n\n[Bridge]\nThey call it a \"Knowledge Transfer\" plan\nI call it the death of a working man\nI am digging the grave with my own two hands\nWhile the shareholders smile in distant lands\nExtracting the ore from inside my head\nLeaving me empty, leaving me dead\n\n[Chorus]\nTrain your replacement\nSign the decree\nGive him the fruit of your memory\nShow him the password, show him the code\nShow him the map of the heavy load\nHe costs a third of what I made a year\nAnd he is the reason that I disappear\nThe H-1B Blues\n\n[Outro]\nHere is your badge.\nGood luck, kid.\nDon't get comfortable."
