      "theory": "The ultimate class consciousness realization: white-collar cognitive professionals and blue-collar industrial trades were never fundamentally different castes—they were merely sequential cohorts in the timeline of capital efficiency. Sitting in an office park parking lot, the displaced son and the discarded father share a thermos of coffee, united in their disposability and solidarity.",
      "summary": "A chaotic, high-energy anthem that serves as the thesis statement of the entire project. It mashes up the organic instrumentation of Act I (Drums, Piano, Guitar) with the digital violence of Act IV (Synths, Distortion, Glitch). The lyrics reject the \"Culture War\" between the rural working class and the urban professional class, exposing it as a distraction. The song argues that whether you wear a hard hat or a headset, if you trade your time for money, you are in the same boat. And that boat is sinking. The Cello plays a frantic, fast-paced melody that weaves the two worlds together.",
      "cleanLyrics": "[Verse 1]\nThey told my daddy he was the salt of the earth\nThen they weighed his labor for exactly what it's worth\nThey stripped the copper wire from the walls of the mill\nAnd left him standing there with a medical bill\nThey told me I was special cause I used my brain\nBut they locked me in the tower with the digital chain\nNow the rust is on the server and the rust is on the gate\nAnd we are both waiting on the same dark fate\n\n[Chorus]\nRed White and Robbed!\nFrom the factory floor to the office mob\nRed White and Robbed!\nIt don't matter if it's a dirty or a clean job\nThey took the pension and they took the stock\nThey put a digital timer on the company clock\nYeah we pledged allegiance to the dollar and the dream\nBut we were just the battery inside the machine\nRed White and Robbed!\n\n[Verse 2]\nYou blame the immigrant I blame the redneck\nBut neither one of us is signing the paycheck\nThey got us fighting in the comments and the street\nWhile they are sitting in the luxury suite\nFrom the blast furnace heat to the server fan whir\nWe were only ever fuel for the engine sir\nThe Algorithm is the Foreman in a new disguise\nAnd it doesn't give a damn about your blue or brown eyes\n\n[Bridge]\nBlue collar (Strike!)\nWhite collar (Strike!)\nNo collar (Strike!)\nIt’s all just labor to them.\nIt’s all just cost to them.\nDelete the worker.\nSave the cash.\nWatch the whole damn system crash!\n\n[Chorus]\nRed White and Robbed!\nFrom the factory floor to the office mob\nRed White and Robbed!\nIt don't matter if it's a dirty or a clean job\nThey took the pension and they took the stock\nThey put a digital timer on the company clock\nYeah we pledged allegiance to the dollar and the dream\nBut we were just the battery inside the machine\nRed White and Robbed!\n\n[Outro]\nWe are the same.\nWe are the same."
